CORE
main.c
--pointer-check --strict-static-array --show-properties
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
^Property read_exact.pointer_dereference.1:$
^  \(signed __CPROVER_bitvector\[65\]\)\(signed long int\)i >= 0 && !\(\(signed __CPROVER_bitvector\[65\]\)\(signed long int\)i >= 4\)$
--
^Property read_exact.pointer_dereference.[2-9][0-9]*:$
^warning: ignoring
--
Checks that exact-size mode emits one dynamic range property instead of the
ordinary decomposed pointer checks.
